.TH ISOFORGE 1 "2026-09-02" "isoforge 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
isoforge \- download Linux images, write them to USB, and build custom installable ISOs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isoforge
[OPTIONS]
.br
.B isoforge
.I command
[COMMAND_OPTIONS]
.br
.B isoforge help
[I command]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Isoforge downloads Linux images from a configured catalog, writes ISO images to USB devices, and builds custom installable ISO images from recipes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B download
Download one or more ISOs from the configured distro catalog.
.TP
.B burn
Write a selected ISO from the configured download directory, or a browsed local ISO, to a selected drive.
.TP
.B build
Build a custom installable ISO from a base image and a recipe.
.TP
.B setup
Install project dependencies.
.TP
.B help
Show top-level help or command-specific help.
.SH TOP-LEVEL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config PATH
Override config file path for the TUI flow.
.TP
.B --version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help and exit.
.SH DOWNLOAD OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config PATH
Override config file path.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show download help and exit.
.SH BURN OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config PATH
Override config file path.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show burn help and exit.
.SH BUILD OPTIONS
.TP
.B -r, --recipe PATH
Recipe to build. Required.
.TP
.B -o, --output DIR
Where to write the ISO. Defaults to \fBdownload_dir\fR from config.json.
.TP
.B --config PATH
Override config file path.
.TP
.B --work-dir DIR
Scratch space for build. Defaults to /var/tmp/isoforge.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Resolve and validate recipe, then stop. Needs no root.
.TP
.B --smoke-test
Boot finished image under QEMU.
.TP
.B --keep
Leave work directory in place for inspection.
.TP
.B --version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show build help and exit.
.SH SETUP PARAMETERS
.TP
.B PACKAGE
Optional package names to install instead of default dependency set.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B download_dir
Directory where downloaded images are saved and where burn scans for .iso files.
.TP
.B distros
Array of \fB{ id, label, url }\fR items shown by download selectors.
.TP
.B block_device_filter
Drive filter used by burn. Use \fBusb\fR for USB/removable devices, or \fBany\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP_DOWNLOADS=1
Allow http:// download URLs from config.json. Disabled by default.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/isoforge/config.json
Default configuration when installed system-wide.
.TP
.I $HOME/Downloads/iso_images
Default download directory used when \fBdownload_dir\fR is missing or empty.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B isoforge --config ./config.json
Run the main TUI using a custom config file.
.TP
.B isoforge download
Download images from configured catalog.
.TP
.B sudo isoforge burn
Write a selected ISO to a selected drive.
.TP
.B sudo isoforge build --recipe recipes/example.yml --dry-run
Validate build recipe without writing an image.
